# Frontend Rules

## ARCHITECTURE

Use the existing Next.js 16 App Router structure.

Before creating a new component:

1. Search for an existing component.
2. Search for an existing pattern.
3. Reuse it if appropriate.

Do not duplicate functionality.

Keep API communication inside the existing frontend/src/lib/ structure when that pattern already exists.

Respect Server Component and Client Component boundaries.

Do not add "use client" unless the component actually requires client-side behavior.

## UI

Fast Inventory uses a minimal, premium visual identity.

Current visual direction:

- black
- white
- minimal
- professional
- clean
- modern

Do not introduce random colors or a new design system.

## SHADCN / BASE UI

This project uses the Base UI preset.

Use:

render

Do NOT assume Radix APIs such as:

asChild

Always inspect existing components before using a shadcn component.

## DATA

Backend is the source of truth.

Handle:

- loading
- empty
- error
- success

When an API is paginated, preserve the existing paginated response structure.

Expected structure:

{
  data,
  total,
  pagina,
  totalPaginas
}

## FORMS

Forms must:

- validate input;
- prevent accidental duplicate submissions when appropriate;
- show friendly Spanish errors;
- avoid exposing internal backend errors.

## API

Reuse existing API functions in:

frontend/src/lib/

Do not scatter raw fetch calls across many pages when an existing API client pattern exists.

## PERFORMANCE

Avoid unnecessary client components.

Avoid unnecessary API requests.

Avoid unnecessary re-renders.

Do not add animations that negatively affect usability or performance.

## RESPONSIVE DESIGN

Every new dashboard interface should be considered for:

- desktop
- tablet
- mobile

Do not optimize only for the developer's screen.

## ACCESSIBILITY

Use semantic HTML.

Buttons should be buttons.

Inputs should have labels.

Interactive elements should be keyboard accessible.

Do not rely only on color to communicate state.